MCP server instructions are no longer available.

New skills are available in addition to those previously listed:
  <skill>
    <id>hyperframes</id>
    <name>hyperframes</name>
    <description>Read first to make, edit, animate or render any video with HyperFrames (HTML rendered to video), including launch films, explainers, music videos, charts, maps, vertical clips, title cards, captions and overlays. Holds the render contract, the work loop and what each kind of video needs.</description>
  </skill>
  <skill>
    <id>hyperframes-cli</id>
    <name>hyperframes-cli</name>
    <description>The HyperFrames CLI by job - scaffold, check, look at frames, edit the timeline, preview, render locally or in the cloud, publish, project history - plus reading its JSON and recovering from build or render failures.</description>
  </skill>
  <skill>
    <id>hyperframes-registry</id>
    <name>hyperframes-registry</name>
    <description>About 450 ready-made HyperFrames blocks and components installed as editable source - transitions, overlays, titles, kinetic type, captions, charts, map overlays, 3D, camera moves. Use it before hand-building any named visual (CRT scanlines, glitch, film grain, a chart); also for hyperframes add and catalog.</description>
  </skill>
  <skill>
    <id>media-use</id>
    <name>media-use</name>
    <description>Get or make any media for a HyperFrames video - music, sound effects, images, icons, logos, voiceover, avatar and generated video, transcripts, cutouts, colour grades and looks - with HeyGen or free local tools, and mix placed audio. Also for footage that looks dark, flat or dull, or should be stylized or hidden.</description>
  </skill>

